# The build context for v2/Dockerfile, whose context is this repository
# root (it builds konturctl out of third_party/kontur and reads the
# commit stamp out of .git, neither of which is under v2/). Nothing else
# in this repo builds from here: packer/kontur's two builds each cd into
# their own directory first, and v2/.dockerignore -- which excludes
# everything -- belongs to Dockerfile.build, whose context is v2/.
#
# .git is deliberately NOT excluded: `go build` stamps bin/grain with the
# commit it came from and can only read that here.

# Build outputs and caches, none of which the image build reads and all
# of which are large: bin/grain is ~200 MB on its own, and shipping a
# host's node_modules would both bloat the context and risk `npm ci`
# resolving against a tree built for a different platform.
v2/bin/
v2/.container-cache/
v2/pkg/ui/frontend/node_modules/
v2/pkg/ui/frontend/test-results/
v2/pkg/ui/frontend/playwright-report/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
